ra  there has been  there was a period of time on the show  where we would much more regularly cover  the overt homophobia school homophobia  from the republican party in the bush  era and in the obama era of the david  pakman show  we were often talking about the  outrageous homophobic tirades on the  floor of the house and on various talk  radio programs by right-wing republicans  it was a much more common thing and in  the trump era there was far less of it  now i'm not saying all of a sudden the  republican party was enlightened on gay  rights that's not what i'm saying at all  what i'm saying is they were less  overtly homophobic because they moved on  to other things including the trans  issue it's important to mention well  very interesting article now in the  texas tribune we failed gay republicans  who fought for acceptance in the texas  republican party see little progress  progress gay republicans who have fought  for acceptance within the texas gop over  the past three decades told the texas  tribune progress has been excruciatingly  slow that's quite an understatement many  of them have left the party even as the  number of log cabin republicans in texas  continues to grow log cabin republicans  is a gay republican group  um and the article sort of tells the  story of how there was this  um a period of time i guess we would say  after the aids crisis  uh where there was the idea that listen  uh we're gay but we want low taxes and  we want low regulation and we're  christian family values whatever and the  republican party is a big tent and  they'll welcome us probably as long as  we have donor dollars and there may have  been a brief period of time where it  seemed like that was a plausible thing  but it has stopped  and um fundamentally what this comes  down to is  there is a group of milli  mostly wealthy white gay men  who think will be accepted as the good  guys as long as we more or less say the  right things they might not love us but  they'll loo